<title>GERMANY: Moksel says rules out dividend for 1997.</title>
<headline>Moksel says rules out dividend for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German meat processing group Moksel AG said on Tuesday it expected 1997 first half group earnings to be slightly negative compared with a 20.9 million mark loss in the 1996 period.</p>
<p>But Moksel said it would not pay a dividend in 1997 and that a payout in 1998 was unlikely despite expectations for break-even results for this year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
